ised end-to-end as a KServe InferenceService backed by a vLLM ROCm serving runtime on AMD Instinct hardware.\n- The report states a go/no-go recommendation with an explicit productization scope (cleared model list) derived from the measured data.\n- The validation environment configuration (node setup, driver versions, device plugin) is documented sufficiently to reproduce the campaign.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware establishing functional and performance parity data for vLLM serving of the supported model set, producing the go/no-go scope for productization.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Hardware access is unresolved: dedicated AMD Instinct nodes require procurement or partner-lab access controlled by parties outside this strategy. The campaign cannot start until access is granted; this is a schedule risk on this epic and everything downstream.\n- Upstream ROCm runtime image cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream communities; the campaign must pin whatever image release is current, and results are specific to that pin.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":31619,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a909e07e0353f612","agent_id":"a6a6c0b0ab8ed134e","session_id":"e98bc21c-3e9c-4db6-bf4b-8cc0fb775cb8","uuid":"ea068e7e-e7f6-4f44-adef-1c7b89df5469","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:37:00.341Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
