urces request `amd.com/gpu` and deploy alongside existing CUDA runtimes in the same cluster without interference.\n- The supported model list for the ROCm runtime is stated and matches the campaign's cleared list.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the models the validation campaign clears.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Upstream ROCm build cadence may not align with platform release trains; mitigation is the recorded image pin plus per-train re-evaluation, not a scope change.\n- The cleared model list is not known until the validation campaign reports; this epic's scope is gated on that report (rewrite: scope shrinks to the cleared models, or descope entirely if no models clear).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":31619,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a909e07e0353f612","agent_id":"a6a6c0b0ab8ed134e","session_id":"e98bc21c-3e9c-4db6-bf4b-8cc0fb775cb8","uuid":"8097f2d8-4f3c-45cf-863a-e2f0f56c3322","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:37:06.152Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
