{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0925dc2842acdfb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n3\ttitle: Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the validation campaign clears fewer models than the supported\n15\t    set, productization scope shrinks to the cleared list; if no models clear, serving\n16\t    productization is descoped and the strategy returns to customers with the parity\n17\t    data as the deliverable.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: -1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 3\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tProductize a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for the model set cleared by the validation campaign's go/no-go report, shipped alongside the existing CUDA runtime builds. Today only CUDA (NVIDIA) builds are productized; ROCm builds exist upstream but are neither shipped nor supported.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Build and release a vLLM ROCm runtime image from the midstream vLLM repository, pinned to a released upstream ROCm base image, released per platform version through the existing build pipeline.\n44\t- Define the ServingRuntime/ClusterServingRuntime resources for the ROCm build, requesting `amd.com/gpu` resources, coexisting with the existing CUDA runtimes in the same cluster.\n45\t- Support exactly the model list cleared by the validation campaign's go/no-go report (the cleared list is an input to this epic, produced by the campaign).\n46\t- Validate the passive KServe surface: KServe InferenceServices deploy and serve predictions with the ROCm runtime under the existing KServe lifecycle (no KServe code changes).\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- The vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized and released per platform version, built from the midstream vLLM repository with its build pipeline green.\n51\t- Every model on the campaign's cleared list serves successfully through a KServe InferenceService backed by the ROCm runtime on AMD Instinct hardware.\n52\t- The runtime image pins a released upstream ROCm base image, and the pin is recorded so it can be re-evaluated against each release train (upstream cadence is externally controlled).\n53\t- The ServingRuntime resources request `amd.com/gpu` and deploy alongside existing CUDA runtimes in the same cluster without interference.\n54\t- The supported model list for the ROCm runtime is stated and matches the campaign's cleared list.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the models the validation campaign clears.\n59\t\n60\t## Risks\n61\t\n62\t- Upstream ROCm build cadence may not align with platform release trains; mitigation is the recorded image pin plus per-train re-evaluation, not a scope change.\n63\t- The cleared model list is not known until the validation campaign reports; this epic's scope is gated on that report (rewrite: scope shrinks to the cleared models, or descope entirely if no models clear).\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af7963df57665428","agent_id":"a472a3df54c9875c3","session_id":"e98bc21c-3e9c-4db6-bf4b-8cc0fb775cb8","uuid":"c00a922e-9cd7-4e8f-b014-82cae720597a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:38:42.348Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-to