b completes with distributed training intact (workers communicate across `amd.com/gpu` devices) on AMD Instinct hardware.\n45\t- A PyTorchJob requesting `amd.com/gpu` is admitted through Kueue queueing when workload queueing is enabled.\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\t- HLR-3 (P1, partial — job/runtime side): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue.\n50\t\n51\t## Risks\n52\t\n53\t- Validation requires access to AMD Instinct hardware (shared dependency with the rest of the strategy's hardware access risk).\n54\t- PyTorch ROCm runtime image availability follows upstream PyTorch ROCm release cadence.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af7963df57665428","agent_id":"a472a3df54c9875c3","session_id":"e98bc21c-3e9c-4db6-bf4b-8cc0fb775cb8","uuid":"93c9f7ce-95a2-4468-a187-bed6787fed5c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:38:44.629Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdd3822d7f5236d0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
