{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc14562c0bf6de00","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n3\ttitle: Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for ROCm workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for ROCm workloads\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tKueue quota handling for AMD GPUs: ClusterQueue/LocalQueue configuration covering `amd.com/gpu` resources so that ROCm training workloads are admitted with correct quota accounting and all-or-nothing gang semantics, matching how NVIDIA GPU quota is handled today.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Define quota configuration (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue resource flavors) that covers `amd.com/gpu` resources on AMD Instinct node pools.\n38\t- Ensure quota accounting and admission — including all-or-nothing (waitForPodsReady) gang semantics — work correctly for workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu`.\n39\t- Cover both single-GPU and multi-GPU job topologies in quota and admission behavior.\n40\t- Verify end-to-end that accelerated jobs requesting `amd.com/gpu` (e.g. PyTorchJobs) are admitted and run on AMD Instinct nodes with quota enforced.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- A ClusterQueue/LocalQueue configuration admits workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu` with correct quota accounting against the configured quotas.\n45\t- All-or-nothing (waitForPodsReady) admission semantics hold for multi-GPU jobs requesting `amd.com/gpu`: a job is admitted only when its full GPU allocation fits.\n46\t- End-to-end: an accelerated job requesting `amd.com/gpu` is admitted through a queue and runs to completion on AMD Instinct nodes with quota enforced.\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\t- HLR-3 (P1, partial — quota/admission side): single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling.\n51\t\n52\t## Risks\n53\t\n54\t- Validation requires access to AMD Instinct hardware (shared dependency with the rest of the strategy's hardware access risk).\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af7963df57665428","agent_id":"a472a3df54c9875c3","session_id":"e98bc21c-3e9c-4db6-bf4b-8cc0fb775cb8","uuid":"f53aeb0c-3122-4bf7-878a-39f6b8c28c74","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:38:45.319Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc14562c0bf6de00","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
