{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b671e6707147102","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E003\n3\ttitle: PyTorch ROCm training support in the Training Operator\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Training Operator\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# PyTorch ROCm training support in the Training Operator\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tSupport PyTorch training on ROCm for single- and multi-GPU jobs run through the Training Operator: PyTorchJobs using PyTorch ROCm runtime images run to completion on AMD Instinct nodes, including multi-GPU and multi-node distributed topologies, with admission through Kueue when workload queueing is enabled.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Enable PyTorchJob workers to run on AMD Instinct nodes: PyTorch ROCm runtime images, `amd.com/gpu` resource requests, and any required node affinity or tolerations for AMD GPU nodes.\n38\t- Verify single-GPU and multi-GPU (including multi-node) PyTorchJob topologies work on ROCm with distributed training intact.\n39\t- Verify PyTorchJobs requesting `amd.com/gpu` are admitted through Kueue when workload queueing is enabled (end-to-end with the platform's queueing layer).\n40\t\n41\t## Acceptance Criteria\n42\t\n43\t- A single-GPU PyTorchJob using a PyTorch ROCm runtime image completes training successfully on AMD Instinct hardware.\n44\t- A multi-GPU PyTorchJob completes with distributed training intact (workers communicate across `amd.com/gpu` devices) on AMD Instinct hardware.\n45\t- A PyTorchJob requesting `amd.com/gpu` is admitted through Kueue queueing when workload queueing is enabled.\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\t- HLR-3 (P1, partial — job/runtime side): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue.\n50\t\n51\t## Risks\n52\t\n53\t- Validation requires access to AMD Instinct hardware (shared dependency with the rest of the strategy's hardware access risk).\n54\t- PyTorch ROCm runtime image availability follows upstream PyTorch ROCm release cadence.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb8502ab256342e0","agent_id":"af63ff59559397d83","session_id":"e98bc21c-3e9c-4db6-bf4b-8cc0fb775cb8","uuid":"afccc304-25dc-4770-8f35-80f469dc6dbb","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:41:53.588Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b671e6707147102","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
