{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d6b7d974dae7a19","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n3\ttitle: AMD Instinct ROCm validation campaign for vLLM serving parity\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -2\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# AMD Instinct ROCm validation campaign for vLLM serving parity\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve the functional and performance parity question for vLLM serving on AMD Instinct accelerators: run a validation campaign on physical AMD GPU hardware covering the supported model set, and produce the go/no-go report that determines the productization scope for a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime. This epic resolves the strategy's central unknown — the platform ships only CUDA runtime builds and has no first-hand parity data for ROCm.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Stand up the validation environment on dedicated AMD Instinct nodes: ROCm driver stack and GPU device plugin exposing `amd.com/gpu` resources, with the environment configuration documented for reproducibility. (Hardware availability itself — procurement or partner-lab access — is an external precondition tracked as a risk, not a deliverable.)\n34\t- Run functional validation: serve each model in the supported model set with a vLLM ROCm runtime build, deployed end-to-end through KServe InferenceServices backed by a ServingRuntime.\n35\t- Run performance validation: measure serving throughput and latency for each model against the CUDA baseline builds, on comparable hardware where available.\n36\t- Produce the go/no-go report: per-model functional pass/fail, performance parity data, and a recommended productization scope (the cleared model list).\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- A validated report exists covering every model in the supported model set, with per-model functional pass/fail results and performance measurements against the CUDA baseline.\n41\t- Each validated model was exercised end-to-end as a KServe InferenceService backed by a vLLM ROCm serving runtime on AMD Instinct hardware.\n42\t- The report states a go/no-go recommendation with an explicit productization scope (cleared model list) derived from the measured data.\n43\t- The validation environment configuration (node setup, driver versions, device plugin) is documented sufficiently to reproduce the campaign.\n44\t\n45\t## HLR Traceability\n46\t\n47\t- HLR-1 (P0): validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware establishing functional and performance parity data for vLLM serving of the supported model set, producing the go/no-go scope for productization.\n48\t\n49\t## Risks\n50\t\n51\t- Hardware access is unresolved: dedicated AMD Instinct nodes require procurement or partner-lab access controlled by parties outside this strategy. The campaign cannot start until access is granted; this is a schedule risk on this epic and everything downstream.\n52\t- Upstream ROCm runtime image cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream communities; the campaign must pin whatever image release is current, and results are specific to that pin.\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b74620e441716e6d","agent_id":"aca7094c6bd436c1b","session_id":"e98bc21c-3e9c-4db6-bf4b-8cc0fb775cb8","uuid":"28b31736-ca0e-468e-bb7c-894f03ea3485","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:42:59.366Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d6b7d974dae7a19","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020"}
