configured quotas.\n45\t- All-or-nothing (waitForPodsReady) admission semantics hold for multi-GPU jobs requesting `amd.com/gpu`: a job is admitted only when its full GPU allocation fits.\n46\t- End-to-end: an accelerated job requesting `amd.com/gpu` is admitted through a queue and runs to completion on AMD Instinct nodes with quota enforced.\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\t- HLR-3 (P1, partial — quota/admission side): single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling.\n51\t\n52\t## Risks\n53\t\n54\t- Validation requires access to AMD Instinct hardware (shared dependency with the rest of the strategy's hardware access risk).\n55\t- The end-to-end admission AC above runs on AMD Instinct nodes whose stand-up (ROCm driver stack, `amd.com/gpu` device plugin) is in scope of the serving validation campaign, which runs in parallel with this epic. Quota/admission verification either shares that environment once it is stood up (coordinate scheduling with the campaign team) or procures its own AMD nodes; either way the node environment itself is not re-delivered here. This is a coordination point, not a blocking dependency — the training work is not gated on serving-parity results.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b74620e441716e6d","agent_id":"aca7094c6bd436c1b","session_id":"e98bc21c-3e9c-4db6-bf4b-8cc0fb775cb8","uuid":"d116ff77-cc4f-4105-95b2-d7f85d604c70","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:43:03.023Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa2c01ac2348a41c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020"}
